			"notes": "- The constructors of classes from the library's API have been made private as they provided no value (and shouldn't have been used due to everything being static).\n- Added documentation for every packet and data class to assist developers in being able to understand how they work :)\n- Added the `RankType` sealed interface which each rank related enum now implements.\n  - This should greatly simplify working across the 3 enums as there is now a concrete common type shared between them.\n  - The sealed nature of the interface enables the use of Java 21's powerful exhaustive pattern matching on all possible enum values which is great for working with the `RankType` type.\n- The `RankType` interface also contains two new static helper methods for working with `RankType`s:\n  - The `getEffectiveRank` method gets the \"effective\" rank out of all 3 enums, see the documentation for more info on the method's behaviour.\n  - The `compare` method is a comparator which allows for comparisons between `RankType` instances to determine which ones are less than/equal to/greater than each other (see documentation for how ranks are compared).\n- Compile against 1.21.1"
		},
